#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aerial-helper -- the ONE backend process of the aerial (network) module.

Contract: docs/contracts/aerial.md section 3. Started as
    setpriv --pdeathsig TERM -- python3 -I tools/aerial/aerial-helper [--bus-address <addr>]
JSON lines out (stdout), commands in (stdin). NetworkManager and BlueZ over D-Bus (python-dbus + GLib), ProtonVPN's CLI and
Proton's server cache, the health pads, the speed test.

THE LAWS THIS FILE KEEPS (CLAUDE.md):
  - every D-Bus call is async (`call()`), so a stuck NetworkManager never stalls the loop; no proxy object is ever made (a proxy
    introspects, which blocks);
  - a program (ping, iw, protonvpn, curl) runs as a child on GLib watches, never as a blocking call;
  - stdin is read from a GLib IO watch, non-blocking; it ends the process on EOF;
  - a turn that raises is caught and logged, and the loop goes on;
  - a secret is printed only by the `secrets` reply; no log line carries a command's arguments;
  - a locked keyring is never opened by a read nobody asked for ("the keyring", below): no prompt because the shell started.
"""
